Make the Mooncake engine-id lookup lazy, so prefill/decode disaggregation works
under Kubernetes service discovery.

THE DEFECT: mooncake_prefill_info -- the map from a prefill worker's base URL
to its Mooncake bootstrap address and per-dp-rank engine ids -- is filled in
exactly one place: VllmPDRouter::new iterates the STATIC --prefill URL list in
its direct-URL branch and queries each entry's bootstrap server once, at
construction (src/routers/http/vllm_pd_router.rs). Under Kubernetes service
discovery that construction path receives an empty static list -- src/server.rs
builds the router with empty prefill and decode lists and no discovery address
-- because workers arrive later, through the watcher in src/service_discovery.rs,
whose add_prefill_server calls never touch the map. The map therefore stays
empty for the life of the process. Every per-request lookup in
get_mooncake_info then misses, logs "No Mooncake bootstrap info for prefill
..., decode will proceed without kv_transfer_params", and the decode request
goes out with no kv_transfer_params at all. The vLLM decoder requires
remote_engine_id, remote_bootstrap_addr and transfer_id together before it
will pull KV blocks, so the transfer never starts -- and nothing fails loudly:
the request is served by the decoder alone, and disaggregation silently does
not happen.

A second defect rides with the first: even where the static list is non-empty,
one query at construction means a prefiller that restarts under a new engine id
is never re-read.

THE FIX: the lookup becomes lazy and per prefill URL. On a cache miss,
get_mooncake_info resolves that prefiller's bootstrap address -- host parsed
from the prefill URL, port read from the worker registry, which already carries
the bootstrap port that Kubernetes discovery stored from the Pod's
vllm.ai/bootstrap-port annotation, falling back to 8998 (the construction
path's own default) -- queries the bootstrap server, and caches the result
under the prefill URL. A failure is not cached, so the next request retries;
that same miss-and-retry is what picks up a prefiller that restarted at the
same URL, and remove_prefill_server now drops the entry so a new owner of the
URL is re-queried rather than trusted from the previous owner's entry. The
retry budget of query_mooncake_bootstrap becomes a parameter: construction
keeps its original 30 attempts, while the request path uses 3 (about three
seconds of backoff) rather than parking a request behind minutes of retries.
This mirrors the shape the llm-d router's sidecar already uses for the same
handshake -- query the bootstrap server inside the request handler, against the
prefill address at hand (llm-d/llm-d-router@v0.10.0,
pkg/sidecar/proxy/connector_mooncake.go).

AGAINST: vllm-project/router v0.1.15 (commit
1fbcde7443d75b36befb61bc081f64c2a1f13a4b), the pin named by
VLLM_ROUTER_VERSION in pack/llm-router/Dockerfile. The defect is present in the
same shape on that project's default branch at the time of writing. The image
build applies this patch with git apply, which fails loudly on a pin whose
hunks no longer match, so a version bump that absorbs or breaks the patch is
detected at build time rather than in a cluster.

UPSTREAM REPORT: NOT YET FILED, and this sentence is where its URL goes. It is
written this way rather than left out because a patch whose report is merely
intended reads, a year later, exactly like one whose report was filed and
ignored. Filing it is what makes carrying this patch a decision with an exit
rather than a fork; until then the exit is named and not yet taken.

TO REFRESH after a pin bump: clone the new pin, git apply this patch, resolve
any rejects, regenerate with git diff, and keep this header on top.

